  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "TTL Limits, Hashed & Wildcard Indexes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No rebuild needed — the window changes in place.",
            "Cannot be compound, cannot sit on `_id`, not on capped collections."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where It Fits"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Use",
            "Why"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "sessions, verification tokens",
              "naturally short lived"
            ],
            [
              "rate-limit counters",
              "window expiry"
            ],
            [
              "event logs, caches",
              "bounded growth"
            ],
            [
              "GDPR retention",
              "hard delete date"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Expired docs can still be returned before the monitor's pass.",
            "Filter defensively in the query when exactness matters.",
            "High-volume time-series: bucket-level expiry beats per-doc deletes."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Prove It Runs",
          "items": [
            "`db.serverStatus().metrics.ttl` exposes `passes`.",
            "And `deletedDocuments` — flat counters mean a dead monitor."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Hashed Indexes",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.u.createIndex({ userId: 'hashed' })",
            "// equality only: NO ranges, NO sorts"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stores a hash of the value instead of the value.",
            "Exists mainly to give an even shard key distribution.",
            "Tames monotonic values like `ObjectId` across chunks."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Wildcard Indexes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`createIndex({'$**':1})` indexes every field path.",
            "`createIndex({'user.$**':1})` scopes it to one subtree.",
            "Suits unpredictable, user-defined schemas.",
            "Cannot be compound (pre-7.0), unique, TTL, or a shard key."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Geo And Clustered"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`{loc:'2dsphere'}` over GeoJSON for `$near`, `$geoWithin`, `$geoIntersects`.",
            "`2d` is legacy flat coordinate pairs — use 2dsphere for anything new.",
            "Clustered collections (5.3+) store docs in `_id` order in the index.",
            "No separate `_id` index, and no FETCH for `_id` lookups."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.u.createIndex({email:1},{",
            "  unique:true,",
            "  partialFilterExpression:{status:'active'}})"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "chain",
          "spec": {
            "title": "index families",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "B-tree",
                "note": "single · compound · multikey"
              },
              {
                "text": "specialised",
                "note": "text · hashed · TTL"
              },
              {
                "text": "schema-free",
                "note": "wildcard"
              },
              {
                "text": "spatial",
                "note": "2dsphere · 2d"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Constraints, explain & the Plan Cache",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Constraint Indexes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`unique`: one doc per key; compound uniqueness is the whole tuple.",
            "`partialFilterExpression` indexes only matching docs — smaller, cheaper.",
            "Partial plus unique is SQL's filtered unique index.",
            "Sparse checks existence only; partial takes any predicate."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Collation Indexes"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.u.createIndex({name:1},",
            "  {collation:{locale:'en', strength:2}})",
            "// case-insensitive; query must match collation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Type",
            "Best at"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Single",
              "ranges + sort"
            ],
            [
              "Compound",
              "multi-field + sort"
            ],
            [
              "Multikey",
              "array membership"
            ],
            [
              "Text",
              "token search"
            ],
            [
              "Hashed",
              "equality + sharding"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Not B-trees At All",
          "items": [
            "TTL: expiry. Wildcard: unknown schema. Geo: spatial.",
            "Columnstore and Atlas Search are separate products.",
            "Neither belongs to the core B-tree family."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "explain Is The Truth",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`explain('executionStats')` is the only real evidence.",
            "`winningPlan` shows what ran; `rejectedPlans` what was weighed.",
            "Health: `nReturned` ≈ `totalKeysExamined` ≈ `totalDocsExamined`.",
            "Big gaps between those three mean wasted work."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Plan Cache"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The planner races candidates over a trial period, caches the winner.",
            "Cached per query shape; re-evaluated after 10x work or index change.",
            "A stale cached plan is why 'it was fast yesterday'."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.coll.getPlanCache().list()",
            "db.coll.getPlanCache().clear()  // last resort"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Predicates That Cannot Seek"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Written",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`/^abc/`",
              "uses the index"
            ],
            [
              "`/abc/`, `/.*abc/`",
              "forced scan"
            ],
            [
              "`$ne`, `$nin`, `$not`",
              "near-full index scan"
            ],
            [
              "`$expr`, `$where`",
              "no index at all"
            ],
            [
              "`{userId:'123'}` vs int",
              "never matches"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Negation, Regex & Pagination Traps",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Why Negation Scans"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`$ne` matches ==everything except one slice== of keys.",
            "The index walks **both** sides of that slice.",
            "Pair it with a selective equality to keep bounds tight."
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Regex Anchors"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "find({name:/^abc/})  // seek",
            "find({name:/abc/})   // scan",
            "find({name:/^abc/i}) // loose bounds"
          ],
          "note": "only an anchored, case-sensitive prefix seeks"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Pagination Traps"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`skip(10000)` still walks 10000 index entries.",
            "Prefer ==range pagination==: `{createdAt:{$lt:lastSeen}}`.",
            "With a supporting index, `sort().limit(10)` stops after **10** keys."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Index Hygiene, Pipelines & Safe Builds",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "MongoDB does not coerce types — `'123'` is not `123`.",
            "`$or` needs an index on EVERY branch or the whole query scans."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Index Hygiene"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.coll.aggregate([{ $indexStats: {} }])",
            "// drop the ones with zero access counts"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Collapse redundant prefixes: `{a}`, `{a,b}`, `{a,b,c}` become one.",
            "`hint()` hides a bad plan and breaks when the data shifts.",
            "Repair the index or the query instead of pinning a hint."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Pipelines And Joins"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Only `$match` and `$sort` at the FRONT of a pipeline use indexes.",
            "Move them before `$group`, `$unwind`, `$project`.",
            "`$lookup` uses an index on the foreign collection's `foreignField`.",
            "Without it, every join is one scan per input document."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Why did latency collapse overnight with no code change?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "`db.coll.totalIndexSize()` outgrew the WiredTiger cache.",
            "Index pages now thrash in from disk on every seek.",
            "Watch the working set, not only the query plan."
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "db.coll.totalIndexSize()",
            "db.serverStatus().wiredTiger.cache"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Building Safely",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Since 4.2 every build is hybrid — no background flag left.",
            "Brief exclusive lock at start and end, yields in between.",
            "On a replica set the build must commit on a majority of nodes.",
            "One node failing aborts the build everywhere."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.currentOp({'command.createIndexes':{$exists:true}})",
            "db.killOp(opid)   // abort a running build"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Rolling Build",
          "text": "Take a secondary out of the set, build, rejoin, repeat, primary last. The zero-impact method for huge production collections."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Inspect, Hide, Drop"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "$indexStats",
              "hidden:true",
              "watch a day",
              "dropIndex"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Pocket Card & the Cost of Writes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Command",
            "Shows"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`getIndexes()`",
              "definitions"
            ],
            [
              "`stats().indexSizes`",
              "bytes per index"
            ],
            [
              "`$indexStats`",
              "usage counts"
            ],
            [
              "`totalIndexSize()`",
              "total footprint"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`db.coll.dropIndex('idx_name')` once the counters stay at zero.",
            "`reIndex()` only on standalone nodes, only to fix corruption.",
            "It locks the collection — never a routine maintenance step.",
            "Keep indexes plus the hot document set inside the cache."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Cache Sizing",
          "items": [
            "Default WiredTiger cache ≈ 50% of RAM minus 1 GB.",
            "Exceed it and index pages thrash from disk."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Pocket Card"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Index `{a:1,b:1,c:1}`",
            "Serves?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`{a}`, `{a,b}`, `{a,b,c}`",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "`{a}` + `sort(b)`",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "`{a,b}` + `sort(c)`",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "`{b}`, `{c}`, `{b,c}`",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "`sort(b)` alone",
              "no"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Direction: single field ignores it; compound matches or full inverse.",
            "ESR: Equality, Sort, Range — decides most compound field orders.",
            "Arrays: auto multikey, one array per index, no covered queries.",
            "TTL: Date only, `expireAfterSeconds`, ~60s, single field, primary.",
            "Text: one per collection, OR-ed terms, `$meta` score, no substrings."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Every Index Costs Writes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Each index adds ==write amplification== to insert, update, delete.",
            "10 indexes means **11** B-tree writes per insert.",
            "Indexes also eat disk and WiredTiger cache RAM."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Before You Add One",
          "text": "Check `$indexStats` for an existing prefix that already serves the query shape."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Plan Stages, ESR & Covered Queries",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Stage Names At A Glance"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Stage",
            "Means"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "COLLSCAN",
              "no index used"
            ],
            [
              "IXSCAN",
              "index seek"
            ],
            [
              "FETCH",
              "loads the full doc"
            ],
            [
              "PROJECTION_COVERED",
              "doc never touched"
            ],
            [
              "SORT",
              "blocking in-memory sort"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Worked Example: ESR",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// find({status:'active',age:{$gt:21}})",
            "//   .sort({createdAt:1})",
            "db.u.createIndex({status:1,createdAt:1,age:1})"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Equality `status` first, sort `createdAt` next, range `age` last.",
            "Wrong order still filters, but adds a blocking SORT stage.",
            "A range opens the slice — nothing after it stays sorted."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Covered Query"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.u.createIndex({email:1,name:1})",
            "db.u.find({email:'a@b.com'},",
            "  {_id:0, name:1})",
            "// totalDocsExamined: 0"
          ],
          "note": "needs _id:0 unless _id is indexed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every read and returned field lives in the index.",
            "Shows ==PROJECTION_COVERED== — the doc is never fetched.",
            "Impossible on a **multikey** index."
          ],
          "style": "check"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Sort Limits, $elemMatch & the Tuning Loop",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Blocking Sort Limit"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "In-memory sorts cap at **100 MB** by default.",
            "Over it: `Sort exceeded memory limit` aborts the query.",
            "`allowDiskUse: true` spills to disk — a bandage, not a fix.",
            "An index in sort order removes the SORT stage."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Direction Test"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Index `{a:1,b:-1}`",
            "Serves?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`sort({a:1,b:-1})`",
              "yes, forward"
            ],
            [
              "`sort({a:-1,b:1})`",
              "yes, backward"
            ],
            [
              "`sort({a:1,b:1})`",
              "no"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The $elemMatch Trap"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "find({items:{$elemMatch:{",
            "  sku:'A', qty:{$gt:5}}}})",
            "// same element must match both"
          ],
          "note": "dot paths can match different elements"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Loop That Works"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.setProfilingLevel(1, {slowms: 100})",
            "// group by query shape, explain the worst,",
            "// add ONE index, then re-measure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "One At A Time",
          "text": "Never guess in batches. One index, one measurement, one decision — a batch hides which change helped and which only added write cost."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 2 of MONGODB INDEXES: A FIELD GUIDE. Your query is either seeking or scanning, and `explain` is the only thing that will tell you which. This field guide walks the whole index zoo — B-tree mechanics, the prefix rule, ESR field order, multikey array traps, TTL, text, and the planner mistakes that quietly turn a seek back into a COLLSCAN. Ten pages of dense notes: save it before your next slow-query hunt.",
